<title>SINGAPORE: ST Computer '96 net profit falls 16.5 pct.</title>
<headline>ST Computer '96 net profit falls 16.5 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>		   (in millions of S$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			   6.33    vs     7.59</p>
<p>    Dividend (cents)		   3.00    vs     3.00</p>
<p>    Group shr (cents)		  6.33    vs     7.59</p>
<p>    Turnover			   327.31    vs   320.96</p>
<p>    Interest income		    0.79    vs     0.54</p>
<p>    Interest expense		   2.73    vs     2.46</p>
<p>    Associates			   0.97    vs    (0.28)</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit		    10.24    vs    11.54</p>
<p>    Tax				    3.10    vs     2.74</p>
<p>    Minorities			  (0.80)   vs    (1.21)</p>
<p>    Extraordinaries		    0.60    vs	nil</p>
<p>Note - ST Computer Systems and Services Ltd, involved in computer and computer-related industries, said the extraordinary item was a gain from an investment disposal by an associate.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703080)</p>
